  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development is of a poor design and would be discordant and highly prominent when viewed from neighbouring properties and the streetscene and would not respect the character of the host dwelling or the wider area, causing harm to the character and appearance of the dwellings and local area. The proposed development is therefore contrary to Policy D3 of the London Plan 2021, Policies CS8, DM10 and DM12 of the Kingston Core Strategy 2012, and Council's Residential Design Supplementary Planning Document 2013.\r\r",
    "The applicant has failed to demonstrate through the submission of cogent information that the proposed extension would not have an adverse impact on the closest ground floor principal habitable room windows at No. 15 Hawks Road in terms of a loss of daylight and sunlight. Given the scale of the extension and the proximity of neighbouring windows, it is considered that there is a likelihood that the development would reduce light entering into the neighbouring habitable room, which in turn would harm the residential amenities of the occupants of the neighbouring property. The excessive depth of the proposed extension would also result in an overbearing and undue sense of enclosure to No. 15 Hawks Road. The proposal is therefore contrary to policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.\r"
  ],
